The '''Slovak Sign Language''' ({{Langx|sk|Slovenský posunkový jazyk}}, '''SPJ''') is the [[sign language]] of the [[deaf]] community in [[Slovakia]]. It belongs to the French sign-language family. Bickford (2005) found that Slovak, [[Czech Sign Language|Czech]], and [[Hungarian Sign Language|Hungarian Sign]] formed a cluster with [[Romanian Sign Language|Romanian]], [[Bulgarian Sign Language|Bulgarian]], and [[Polish Sign Language|Polish Sign]].<ref>Bickford, 2005. [http://www.sil.org/silesr/2005/silesr2005-026.pdf ''The Signed Languages of Eastern Europe'']</ref>

Despite the similarity of oral Slovak and Czech, SSL is not particularly close to [[Czech Sign Language]].{{Citation needed|date=May 2022}}

